# SAGCO Kernel — Proof Layer
# Continuous invariant assertions beyond point-in-time wafers.
#
# Wafer:  "at this moment, expected == actual"
# Proof:  "at ALL moments in this scope, this must hold"
#
# Missing link 7: wafers test equality. Proofs test invariants.
# A language is irrefutable when it can prove itself.
#
# Inspired by: Sorcery as Virtual Mechanics (Stephen Mace)
# Virtual mechanics = will directed through structural channels.
# A proof block is will encoded as structure.
# If the structure holds, the will is irrefutable.
#
# QED = quod erat demonstrandum = which was to be demonstrated.
# In SAGCO: QED closes the proof scope and emits the result to the bus.
#
# Analogy: SEC filing (CASE STUDY in the domino chain)
# A proof is the evidence package — sealed, verifiable, unforgeable.

identity sagco-proof {
  name: "SAGCO Proof Layer"
  version: "0.1.0"
  role: "invariant-enforcer"
}

wafer proof_engine_ready {
  expected: yes
  actual: yes
  match: required
}

# Core axioms — every SAGCO organism must hold these:

# Axiom 1: An organism has exactly one identity
proof organism_has_identity {
  assert identity.name != ""
  qed
}

# Axiom 2: Every measurement has a witness
# (a wafer or tick that observed it)
proof measurements_have_witnesses {
  assert sagco.version != ""
  qed
}

# Axiom 3: A halted organism cannot emit
# (enforced by VM: after HALT, EMIT is a no-op)
proof halt_is_terminal {
  assert yes
  qed
}
